WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.160
SPEAKER: It's officially
week seven of "Google Cloud

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.190
Next" on air, which
means we're focusing

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.350
on application modernization.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.600
I'm Stephanie Wong, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.050
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.020
Week 7 is all about
application modernization.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.880
And we all know
that phrase means

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.220
something different to
pretty much everyone.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.040
So this week, we've got
five tracks of content,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.780
each packed with sessions.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.930
Whether you want to learn more
about containers, serverless,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.132
app development, cost
management, or ops and SRE,

00:00:31.132 --> 00:00:32.549
you're bound to
find something you

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.480
like in this session catalog.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.390
So take the time
to browse this week

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.180
and add interesting sessions
to your playlist, where

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.400
you can watch them on demand.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.260
This week, we're
shining the spotlight

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.270
on serverless functions,
which demonstrates

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.250
how to use Cloud
Functions to create

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.700
standalone functions that
can respond to cloud events

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.650
without the need
to manage a server.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.570
And if you're looking
for inspiration

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.090
on the possibilities of
functions as a service,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.130
you'll enjoy IKEA's
firsthand account

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.850
of how they used Cloud Functions
to create complex applications

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.750
and workflows.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.640
I added enhancing
collaboration to my playlist,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.860
because I like the
idea of using Python

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.670
to bring my GCP functions into
a convenient place like Google

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.570
Sheets.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.280
By creating custom
functions, I can

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.530
make it easy for
anyone in the company

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.020
to use the GCP
solutions I build.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.660
So if you want to learn more
about how Python can bridge

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.630
GCP and Google Sheets to
enhance collaboration,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.930
then be sure to add this
one to your playlist.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.530
Finally, our team is so excited
to be hosting the developer

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.280
keynote.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.340
You can hear directly from
the VP of developer relations,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.440
and then stay tuned
for demos from some

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.940
of my favorite co-workers.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.470
We look forward to
the dev keynotes.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.460
Because seeing what is possible
with GCP is always inspiring.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.100
And we hope you'll leave this
keynote with your mind spinning

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.600
with ideas.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.820
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.210
check out the link.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.260
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.740
Leave us a comment, or
tweet us using the hashtag

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.030
#googlecloudnext.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.930
And we'll see you in the cloud.

